@startuml client_send_queue_send_activity
title ClientSendQueue - sending without a reply

start
:Send(message);
if (message.size() > max_send_size_?) then (yes)
    :Return EMSGSIZE;
    stop
else (no)
    :Lock lifetime_.mutex_;
endif
:Create ClientConnectionLifetime::Operation;
if (Operation rejected admission?) then (yes)
    :End rejected operation scope and unlock;
    :Return EINVAL;
    stop
else (no)
    :Retain the admitted operation;
endif
if (truly_async or (fully_ordered and reply slot engaged)?) then (yes)
    :TryQueue(message, empty callback);
    :Select acceptance or ENOBUFS from admission;
else (direct)
    :Create a live local ReplySlotToken;
    if (fully_ordered?) then (yes)
        :Reserve waiting_for_reply_ and identify this marker as owner;
    else (no)
        :Leave reply sequencing independent of this send;
    endif
    :SendTransport(operation, SEND, message);
    if (This sender still owns the marker?) then (yes)
        :Reset the reply slot and its owner;
        :ArmIfNeeded();
    else (no)
        :Preserve another path's reservation;
    endif
    :Select the transport result;
endif
:End Operation scope and unlock;
:Return the selected result;
stop

legend
    Transport delegates to Operation::Execute and runs outside the mutex.
    A direct ordered marker lets concurrent admission queue during IPC.
    Default unordered one-way sends do not wait behind a pending reply.
    Local queue acceptance is not confirmation of peer receipt.
endlegend

@enduml